## Creating Test Runs (Complete Procedure)

**Naming convention:** `console-{component}-acm{version}-sprint{NN}-{JIRA-ID}`

Examples:
- `console-clusters-acm217-sprint03-ACM-32280`
- `console-alc-acm217-sprint02-ACM-32876`
- `console-search-acm217-sprint02-ACM-24962`

**Component values:** `clusters`, `alc`, `search`, `grc`, `credentials`, `virt`, `rbac`

**One test run per dev story** (not per epic or per test case).

### Step-by-step procedure:

```
# 1. Find the correct plan ID
list_polarion_plans(project_id="RHACM4K", query="name:2.17", status="open")
# Look for: ACM_2_17_Sprint_3 (or whichever sprint)

# 2. Create the test run WITH plan_id
create_polarion_test_run(
  project_id="RHACM4K",
  test_run_id="console-{component}-acm217-sprint{NN}-ACM-{ID}",
  title="Console {Component} - {Feature Title}",
  plan_id="ACM_2_17_Sprint_3",
  custom_fields_json='{"type": "featureVerification", "jiraid": "ACM-{ID}"}'
)

# 3. Upload test results (adds test cases to the run)
upload_polarion_test_results(
  project_id="RHACM4K",
  test_run_id="console-{component}-acm217-sprint{NN}-ACM-{ID}",
  results_json='[{"test_case_id": "RHACM4K-XXXXX", "result": "passed", "comment": "..."}]'
)
```

### Fields set via MCP:
- `test_run_id` (naming convention)
- `title`
- `plan_id` → sets "Planned In" (MUST pass at creation time)
- `type` → "featureVerification"
- `jiraid` → the dev story (e.g., "ACM-32280")
- Test case results (passed/failed/blocked with comments)

### Fields that MUST be set manually in Polarion UI:
- **Squad** → "Console" (no MCP field for this)
- **Planned In** (if not passed at creation via plan_id -- can't be updated after)

### Limitations:
- No `update_test_run` tool exists -- plan_id MUST be passed at creation time
- Squad field cannot be set via MCP custom_fields_json (Polarion rejects it)
- If plan_id is missed at creation, user must set "Planned In" manually in Properties tab
- ALWAYS pass `plan_id` at creation to avoid manual step

## After Creating a Test Run: Update the QE JIRA Ticket

Every dev story has a QE tracking ticket (e.g., `[QE] --- ACM-32282: ...`). After creating a test run, update the QE ticket's description to mark completion and add the Polarion link.

**QE ticket description template (JIRA wiki markup):**
```
Note: If analysis and review is done and no QE effort is required, the task can be closed.

Completion checklist
[X] - Test cases created in Polarion and referenced [here|https://polarion.engineering.redhat.com/polarion/#/project/RHACM4K/workitem?id=RHACM4K-XXXXX]
[ ] - Test cases are reviewed and approved
[X] - Test runs executed in Polarion and referenced [here|https://polarion.engineering.redhat.com/polarion/#/project/RHACM4K/testrun?id=console-{component}-acm217-sprint{NN}-ACM-{ID}]
```

**Rules:**
- Replace `[ ]` with `[X]` for completed items
- The `[here|URL]` syntax is JIRA wiki markup for a hyperlink
- Test case link points to the Polarion work item (RHACM4K-XXXXX)
- Test run link points to the Polarion test run (the ID you just created)
- Use `update_issue(issue_key, description=...)` to update the QE ticket
- Find the QE ticket via: `search_issues(jql="summary ~ '[QE]' AND summary ~ 'ACM-{story-id}'")`
- ALWAYS verify the link is correct (single URL, no duplicates) before updating
